# Shared DEV config (committed; Vite loads it only in `vite dev`, never in the
# production/demo build or under vitest's `test` mode), so every dev checkout
# behaves the same without a per-machine env file.
#
# The backend now allows localhost (CORS fixed), so the browser talks to it
# DIRECTLY — no dev proxy. The migrated features (VITE_LIVE_APIS) hit the real
# backend; MSW still runs in dev (the built-in default) to serve the features
# the backend hasn't built yet — Programs content, Chat, and the Plan Workspace.
# Those stay mocked until their endpoints exist; the rest is real.
#
# To run everything on mocks instead (fully offline), override in a gitignored
# .env.development.local with: VITE_LIVE_APIS=
VITE_API_URL=https://nws-api.underdev.in/api/v1
VITE_LIVE_APIS=auth,clients,nutritionists,dashboard
